{"baseline": "reliable", "correlation_id": "eec8cc18-67a7-4b06-92ef-16705de2f313", "event": "message_received", "group_id": "s6102_reviewer", "instance": "reviewer-7101", "model": "qwen2.5:7b", "offset": 31, "partition": 0, "payload": {"correlation_id": "eec8cc18-67a7-4b06-92ef-16705de2f313", "draft": "A move-in inspection checklist documents the initial condition of a rental property, protects both tenants and landlords by providing a clear record, and facilitates a fair comparison at the end of the tenancy.", "from_stage": "writer", "input_source": {"offset": 11, "partition": 0, "topic": "s6102_tasks"}, "plan": "A move-in inspection checklist serves to document the condition of a rental property at the start of a tenancy. Here are three short steps:\n\n1. **Document Initial Condition**: List all aspects of the property, such as walls, floors, appliances, and fixtures, noting any existing damage or wear.\n2. **Protect Tenants and Landlords**: Provide a clear record for both tenants and landlords regarding the property's state, helping to avoid disputes over repairs or maintenance at the end of the tenancy.\n3. **Facilitate Move-Out Inspection**: Use the initial checklist as a basis for comparing conditions at the end of the tenancy, ensuring a fair assessment of any necessary repairs or cleaning.", "question": "Explain the purpose of a move-in inspection checklist.", "rental_context": {"data_version": 12, "dataset_id": "0e586d72da6211f1ae011ab4cc3919df", "listings": [], "requested_codes": []}, "run_id": "question-eec8cc18-67a7-4b06-92ef-16705de2f313", "writer_instance": "writer-7100"}, "pid": 7101, "raw_bytes": 1377, "run_id": "question-eec8cc18-67a7-4b06-92ef-16705de2f313", "source_commit": "52c8ef470b124605a0fc51dd8c5821b4a5f3738b", "stage": "reviewer", "student": "Pragya Apurva", "timestamp": "2026-11-07T04:25:37.035325+00:00", "topic": "s6102_drafts"}
